awavedat.inp
*  In case option 2, specify hereafter NHT=number of conditions
*    NHT
*     2
*   In case option 2, specify hereafter wave height Hrms , T and TETA as functio
*   interpolated linearly at each time step (if end time is smaller than total
*   computation time, the cycle is repeated)
*    TIME(s) HRMS    T   TETA W10
*                               TIME = duration (s)
*                               Hrms = RMS wave height (m)
*                               T    = wave period (s)
*                               TETA = anle of wave incidence to normal (pos. or
*                               W10
*   0.         0.01    5.   0.  0.
*   72000.     0.01    5.   0.  0.
*  Parameters for hydrodynamics (friction, breaking, currents)
*
*  Switch1 0/1; 0=velocity asymmetry Isobe-Horikawa; 1= Ruessink 2008
*  ROller-coefficient (0=maximum roller effect; 1.= no roller; default=0.5)
*  COEF6=distance for averaging of wave parameters in undertow model; 3 field cases; 1 lab cases 
*  CLH= coefficient for Longuet-Higgins streaming near the bed (0-1)
*  CSW= coefficient to include effective swash velocity near water line for shingle beach (0-1)
*  Switch2 0/1; 0=excl. acceleration effect on shear stress,  1=incl. acceleration effect of Nielsen
*  Switch3 0/1; 0=excl. phase lag effects for wave-related susp. transport, 1= incl phase lags
*  SL=Maximum slope angle of dune front (in degrees); sliding occurs if local bed angle is larger
*  SEF=suspension enhancement factor=1 to 2; 1 without dune erosion; 2 for dune erosion
*  Switch4 0/1 (integer); o=excluding long waves in surf zone; 1= incl.
*
*  Switch1 ROLLERcoef  COEF6  CLH  CSW  Switch2  Switch3  SL   SEF  Swithch4 
      1        0.5       1.     1.  1.     0       0      50    1.   1
*
*  COEFSR=coefficient roller shear stress at water surface (0=default, gives zero stress)
*  GAMMA=breaking index (0=default,computed by model; otherwise specify value 0.
*  ELS=horizontal mixing coefficient for longshore current (0.1 to 3 m2/s);
*  COEF5= parameter related to averaging of wave height and  depth for long. current;
*         3 for field cases; 1 for lab cases
*  ELS=horizontal mixing coefficient for longshore current (0.1 to 10 m2/s);
*  Niteration=number of iterations for longshore velocities (=1 if TETA=0)
*  SW=0.01 to 0.2= extra smoothing near waterline (over 10 points on both sides of last point)
*  COEFSR  GAMMA  coef5   ELS(m2/s)    Niteration   SW
   0.       0      1.      0.5            300       0.2       
*  options output transport 0/1/2 and NOUT
*  0= no output transport; 1=summed over classes; 2= transport per class
*  NOUT= output of bed levels after any NOUT time steps
    2  3
*   Sediment transport parameters
*   DL   = thickness of active transport layer (m) ( 0.2 to 1)
*   RHOS = sediment density (2650 kg/m3)
*   POR  = porosity of bed ( 0.4 )
*   facbed= calibration factor bed load transport (default=1)
*   facsusc= calibration factor current-related susp.load transport (default=1)
*   facsusw= calibration factor wave-related susp.load transport (default=1)
*   T-END= total computation time (s)
*   DL(m)  RHOS(kg/m3) POR(-) facbed (-) facsusc (-) facsusw (-) T-END (s)
      0.25    2650      .4     1.0        1.0          1.0    86400.
*   
*   factime;  DT=factime*3600 seconds if 0<Hrms,off<1 m
*             DT=factime*2400         if 1<Hrms,off<2 m 
*              DT=factime*1200         if 2<Hrms,off<3 m 
*              DT=factime*600          if 3<Hrms,off<3.5 m 
*              DT=factime*300          if 3.5<Hrms,off<4 m 
*              DT=factime*200          if 4<Hrms,off<4.5 m 
*              DT=factime*100          if Hrms,off<4.5 m 
*   facbed;   Smoothing-bed=facbed*0.005; facbed may be as large as 500
*   facgrain; Smoothing-fractions=facgrain*0.2
*   factime   facbed      facgrain
    0.25          0.2            1
